      content: `**Adult patients with corrected or uncorrected congenital heart defects possess highly rigid, lesionspecific physiology with limited compliance and minimal functional reserves. They have an increased dependence on preload and are highly sensitive to sudden drops in systemic afterload. Right ventricular dysfunction is common; avoid factors that elevate pulmonary vascular resistance (PVR): **pain, acidemia, hypoxemia, hypercapnia, hypothermia, and excessive positive airway pressures/PEEP** (which compress pulmonary capillaries and restrict venous return). Maintain sinus rhythm and optimize right ventricular perfusion pressure.**`
